<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cảnh Thịnh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1783–1802</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Canh Thinh, Nguyễn Quang Toản</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cảnh Thịnh, born Nguyễn Quang Toản, was the second emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tay-son-dynasty">Tây Sơn dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quang-trung">Quang Trung</a> as a boy in 1792. His court was weakened by factional purges and quarrels with his uncle's southern realm. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gia-long">Nguyễn Ánh</a> took Phú Xuân in 1801 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thăng Long</a> in 1802, and Cảnh Thịnh was captured and executed.</p></div>
